  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Erythema Multiforme through a chain of indications that link it to Methylprednisolone, a corticosteroid with similar pharmacological properties. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone, through its indication for Chronic Beryllium Disease, is indirectly connected to Erythema Multiforme via Methylprednisolone, which is also indicated for the same condition. This pathway highlights a potential role of corticosteroids in triggering Erythema Multiforme, possibly through immunomodulatory effects. The overlapping indications between Dexamethasone and Methylprednisolone suggest a shared mechanism of action, possibly involving the suppression of inflammatory responses. While the direct causal link between Dexamethasone and Erythema Multiforme remains unclear, the evidence supports a broader role of corticosteroids in the development of this condition, emphasizing the importance of corticosteroid use in clinical settings where Erythema Multiforme is observed.",
